1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:09,101
When x is small, x squared is tiny and x cubed tinier still, so the first two or three terms already give an excellent value.

2
00:00:09,101 --> 00:00:18,632
One point zero two to the power one third: one, plus point zero two over three, minus point zero zero zero four over nine.

3
00:00:18,632 --> 00:00:23,554
The next term is about a millionth and cannot touch the fifth decimal place.

4
00:00:23,554 --> 00:00:26,705
One point zero zero six six two.

